 "name": "H3V3LD5B",
 "kind": "tvs",
 "manufacturer": "Zhuhai Hongjiacheng Technology",
 "title": "Bidirectional 3.3 V low-capacitance ESD protection diode, SOD-523",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev 2.1",
  "pages": 3
 },
 "summary": "A two-terminal bidirectional TVS diode that guards a low-voltage signal line against ESD and surge, in the small SOD-523 package. It stands off 3.3 V in either polarity, breaks down between 3.5 V and 6.5 V, leaks at most 0.2 µA, and presents 12.5 pF typical. It withstands ±25 kV air and ±20 kV contact discharge to IEC 61000-4-2 and an 8 A 8/20 µs surge to IEC 61000-4-5, clamping to 12 V or less at that current. Uses named for it: handsets and their accessories, PDAs, notebooks and handhelds, digital cameras and portable instruments, peripherals, audio players and industrial equipment.",
